    <!-- TAB 2: ABSTRACT REVIEW -->
    <section id="section-abstracts" class="hidden space-y-6">
      <!-- How many abstracts have their full author list, with a filter for
           the rest. renderAbstractsAuthorsSummary(). -->
      <div id="abstracts-authors-summary" class="hidden flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 rounded-xl border border-gold-300 bg-gold-50 px-4 py-3"></div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Step 1 · Approval</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Accept or reject each submission. Once accepted, it moves to Step 2 below; Reset in its review brings it back here.</p>
        <div id="abstracts-approval-container" class="space-y-4"></div>
      </div>
      <!-- Hidden entirely for a role without abstracts.assign (see
           applyRoleVisibility). The id is on the whole block, not just the
           list, so the heading and blurb go with it rather than leaving a
           section that explains an action you cannot take. -->
      <div id="abstracts-assignment-block" class="pt-4 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Step 2 · Assignment (approved abstracts)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Assign oral, poster or award presentation. The delegate's decision email is sent from here; once it has gone, the format is fixed and the abstract moves to Step 3.</p>
        <div id="abstracts-assignment-container" class="space-y-4"></div>
      </div>
      <!-- Step 3, presentations (renderPresentations()): each presenter
           uploads their e-poster or paper in the portal by the last date;
           here, what has come in, the files, and the email to presenters. -->
      <div id="abstracts-presentations-block" class="pt-4 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Step 3 · Presentations</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Each presenter uploads their e-poster or paper in the portal, on the Abstract card, by the last date. Files are named registration no_name_type (e.g. NQOCN20260045_Asha_Patil_Poster.pdf). The guidelines and templates: <a href="/website/presentations" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-semibold text-indigo-700 underline">Presentation guidelines</a>.</p>
        <div id="presentations-head" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-3"></div>
        <div id="presentations-chips" class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mb-3" role="group" aria-label="Show presentations"></div>
        <div id="presentations-list" class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl divide-y divide-slate-100"></div>
      </div>
      <!-- Step 4, poster screens (renderPosterScreens()): every e-poster
           whose decision has been sent gets a screen and a place in its
           running order; the time follows from the poster session. -->
      <div id="abstracts-screens-block" class="pt-4 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Step 4 · Poster screens</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Every e-poster whose decision has been sent gets a screen and a place in its running order. Times follow from the session's start and the minutes per poster. Move a poster with its arrows and Screen menu, or drag it on a laptop. Presenters see their screen and time in the portal once you switch it on.</p>
        <div id="screens-settings" class="mb-3"></div>
        <div id="screens-fit" class="mb-3"></div>
        <div id="screens-actions" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-3"></div>
        <div id="screens-chips" class="flex gap-2 overflow-x-auto -mx-4 px-4 sm:mx-0 sm:px-0 mb-3 lg:hidden" role="group" aria-label="Show screen"></div>
        <div id="screens-board" class="grid gap-3 grid-cols-1 lg:[grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(230px,1fr))]"></div>
        <div id="screens-unallotted" class="mt-3"></div>
      </div>
      <!-- Step 5, Zenodo (abstracts.publish only, and only while it is
           switched on in Conference setup › Zenodo; renderZenodo()): accepted
           abstracts whose presenting author agreed, sent as drafts with the
           DOI reserved, then published -- which cannot be undone. -->
      <div id="abstracts-zenodo-block" class="hidden pt-4 border-t border-slate-200">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 uppercase tracking-wide">Step 5 · Publish with DOIs (Zenodo)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Only accepted abstracts whose presenting author agreed in the portal, and who has registered. Send as a draft to check it on Zenodo with its DOI reserved, then publish. A published record and its DOI are permanent.</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mb-3">Settings and the on/off switch: <button type="button" onclick="openSetupPage('zenodo')" class="font-semibold text-indigo-700 underline">Conference setup › Zenodo</button>. <span id="zenodo-status"></span></p>
        <div id="zenodo-summary" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-3"></div>
        <div id="zenodo-list" class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl divide-y divide-slate-100"></div>
      </div>
    </section>
